  "track.runtime.b9.title": "The Android host, semantics and accessibility",
  "track.runtime.b9.essence": "The host connects Compose to the View and window lifecycle.\nThe semantics tree is a parallel tree that serves accessibility and testing.\n`Owner` and `AndroidComposeView` are Android implementation details, not app APIs.",
  "track.runtime.b9.goal.g1": "Saw how the semantics tree is merged",
  "track.runtime.b9.goal.g2": "Compared the two tree consumers",
  "track.runtime.b9.sec.sem.title": "Merged and unmerged",
  "track.runtime.b9.sec.sem.badge": "stable",
  "track.runtime.b9.sec.sem.p.1": "Foundation and Material components fill in semantics automatically; low-level custom composables must declare their own. `Button`, `clickable` and `toggleable` merge their descendants. Accessibility services use the unmerged tree and merge it themselves; the testing framework uses the merged tree by default, with `useUnmergedTree` to switch. [[src:cp-semantics]]",
  "track.runtime.b9.sec.sem.p.2": "Accessibility does not \"go only through the Owner\": on Android, the host part connects the semantics tree to the accessibility system, but the same tree is used by the testing framework. `Owner` and `AndroidComposeView` are labelled [[badge:android-impl]].",
  "track.runtime.b9.sec.sem.p.3": "WCAG, inclusive design and semantics in Compose meet in bridge X6 (chapter E10).",
  "track.runtime.b9.quiz.q1.q": "Which tree does the testing framework use by default?",
  "track.runtime.b9.quiz.q1.a": "The merged tree.",
  "track.runtime.b9.quiz.q1.why": "You can switch to the unmerged tree with `useUnmergedTree = true`.",
  "track.runtime.b9.quiz.q2.q": "Is `AndroidComposeView` an API for apps to call?",
  "track.runtime.b9.quiz.q2.a": "No.",
  "track.runtime.b9.quiz.q2.why": "It is an implementation detail of Compose UI on Android.",
  "track.runtime.b10.title": "Live Runtime Explorer: the +1 flow",
  "track.runtime.b10.essence": "Start with `count = 0`; tap `+1` and walk eight steps from the handler to the phases.\nEach step shows the state before and after, the component at work, the affected scope or phase, the UI tree change and what was skipped.\nChange the start value and the `Header` parameter to see steps 6 and 7 recomputed.",
  "track.runtime.b10.goal.g1": "Reached the Recomposer step",
  "track.runtime.b10.goal.g2": "Walked all eight steps",
  "track.runtime.b10.sec.flow.title": "The whole path",
  "track.runtime.b10.sec.flow.badge": "simplified",
  "track.runtime.b10.sec.flow.p.1": "User event → write to `MutableState` → Snapshot records it; scopes that read the state may be invalidated → the Recomposer coordinates → transformed composable code re-runs at the needed scope → the Composer compares and decides to update or skip → the Applier applies to the UI tree → Compose UI runs the needed phases → the semantics tree serves accessibility and testing.",
  "track.runtime.b10.sec.flow.p.2": "The eight steps are a teaching split; the real runtime batches and optimises differently. The Reset, Previous, Next, Play, Pause and speed controls are below the diagram.",
  "track.runtime.b10.quiz.q1.q": "In step 7, when does the Applier insert a new node?",
  "track.runtime.b10.quiz.q1.a": "When the structure changes: count going from 0 to 1 makes the `if (count > 0)` branch appear.",
  "track.runtime.b10.quiz.q1.why": "From 5 to 6 there is only a text update.",
  "track.runtime.b10.quiz.q2.q": "Why is `Header(title = \"Counter\")` skipped?",
  "track.runtime.b10.quiz.q2.a": "Its parameter is stable and equal to last time.",
  "track.runtime.b10.quiz.q2.why": "See the rule in B8.",
  "track.runtime.cap.map": "A map of the 11 parts of the Compose Runtime (isometric blocks). Click a block (or pick it in the \"Component\" box) to see what it does; the highlighted block is the part being discussed.",
  "track.runtime.cap.setcontent": "Left to right: setContent creates a Composition, compiled code runs in the Composer, the result is written to the slot table and through the Applier into the UI tree, then the phases run. The highlighted card is the step running now.",
  "track.runtime.cap.compiler": "The @Composable function, after the compiler transforms it, is run by the Composer and recorded in the slot table. The token shows where data just went.",
  "track.runtime.cap.snapshot": "A read–write loop: the Composer reads state inside a snapshot; when the state changes, the snapshot notifies the Recomposer, which schedules the part of the Composition that read that state to run again.",
  "track.runtime.cap.recomposer": "Left to right: a state write → the Recomposer batches changes until the next frame → the Composition re-runs the affected part → the Applier applies the changes to the UI tree.",
  "track.runtime.cap.applier": "The Composer records results in the slot table (top) and sends commands to the Applier (bottom); the Applier inserts, removes, moves or updates nodes in the UI tree.",
  "track.runtime.cap.counter": "One tap on the counter goes round a full loop: the UI tree receives the click → state is written in a snapshot → Recomposer → Composition → Composer → Applier → UI tree and phases. Follow the highlighted card round the loop.",
  "track.runtime.cap.keys": "The list on top, its positions below. The state on each card says whether the item is kept, recomposed, created or leaves the Composition when the list changes.",
  "track.runtime.cap.phases": "State on the left; the three phases Composition, Layout and Drawing on the right. Where the state is READ decides which phase has to run again (highlighted card).",
  "track.runtime.cap.skip": "The parent composable on top, the child below. The child state says whether it is recomposed or skipped this time.",
  "track.runtime.fam.idle": "not running at this step",
  "track.runtime.fam.run": "running / running again",
  "track.runtime.fam.done": "done / kept",
  "track.runtime.cap.semantics": "The UI tree produces the semantics tree; the semantics tree serves screen readers and tests."
